test_cv_dual_dump_keyword -- cv_dual | matbld on LaGriT's dump commands (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_dump_keyword_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]   8 cases, about 2 s
  open summary.html

  (cv_dual is the one beside lagrit: build/cv_dual)

WHAT IS TESTED

  dump / stor, dump / fehm, dump / pflotran and dump / zone_outside
  take the keyword cv_dual or matbld (src/dump_cv_dual.f90, called by
  writedump.f). cv_dual is the default since V3.4.0; matbld is LaGriT's
  earlier code, as before. With cv_dual the .stor (stor, fehm), the .uge
  (pflotran) and the boundary
  areas (_outside_vor.area, _med, _hyb: fehm, zone_outside) come from
  cv_dual on the mesh object, with voronoi (default), median or hybrid
  control volumes. Each case is a LaGriT deck, NAME.lgi, run in
  work/NAME; the deck writes the mesh with dump / avs (mesh.inp) before
  the dump commands. Then the cv_dual program runs on mesh.inp once per
  argument list of the case (work/NAME/prog1, prog2, ...), with
  -outside_area to list each boundary vertex's vector area.

  d01 dump / stor on a moved lattice of tets: compressed, none and
      nofilter_zero; no keyword and cv_dual give the same file; matbld
      by name.
  d02 dump / fehm on LaGriT's Poisson disk mesh in a box: voronoi,
      median, hybrid against matbld (and matbld's keepatt_median).
  d03 dump / pflotran: filter_zero (default) and nofilter_zero.
  d04 2D triangles: dump / fehm and dump / pflotran.
  d05 a dfnWorks fracture network: dump / fehm.
  d06 dump / zone_outside: voronoi, and hybrid with keepatt_voronoi
      (the areas follow the control volumes; xn_harea ... kept).
  d07 options cv_dual does not have (vector, both, pflotran verbose):
      matbld writes the dump, with one line saying so; a keyword as
      the sixth token of dump / fehm.
  d08 the default (no keyword): a hex mesh goes to matbld (with a
      line); a mesh that is not Delaunay and one with parent/child
      chains give an ERROR naming / matbld, and nothing is written;
      with / matbld (and / median) they are written.
  er01 six commands that must fail: median without cv_dual, cv_dual
      with matbld, two kinds of control volumes, median with binary,
      dump / fehm on a mesh that is not Delaunay and on hexes.

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_dump_keyword.py; cases.txt lists each case's)

  ran        LaGriT ran the whole deck (after.inp exists)
  errors     the number of "ERROR: dump/" lines
  message    each text cases.txt names is in LaGriT's output
  nothing    no file named bad* (the failing commands' outputs)
  progK      each file program run K wrote equals the deck's, byte for
             byte, the .stor's line 2 aside, which must end with
             (cv_dual dump / ...), the command
  eq         two roots' files equal byte for byte (matbld by name and
             not; a fallback and plain matbld)
  zones      the geometry and zone files equal matbld's byte for byte
  areaeq     boundary areas equal matbld's to their 13 digits
             (Voronoi, median)
  arealist   each vertex's boundary area in LaGriT's zone and area files
             equals the program's outside_area list
  boxsum     on a box each side's signed areas along its normal add up
             to its area (a uniform infiltration sums exactly), for
             every kind of control volume
  att, exists, cvline2   an attribute kept, a file written, a .stor's
             line 2

  The meshes come from other suites: test_cv_dual_dfn (full_mesh.inp),
  test_cv_dual_poisson_lagrit (test_3d_poi_01.inp) and
  test_cv_dual_delaunay's generator (flip3d.inp, made in work/gen).

WHAT WAS FOUND (Nov 18 2026)

  - Voronoi boundary areas: LaGriT's get_xcontab splits each boundary
    triangle at its own circumcenter; cv_dual's Voronoi control volumes
    meet the boundary at the same points. The two agree to rounding
    (1e-16 on the Poisson mesh), and so do the median ones (thirds).
    In 2D and on a fracture's edges both give each vertex half of each
    boundary edge.
  - dump / fehm took its sixth token as an FEHM .ini file to read
    unless it was -def-: dump / fehm / root / mo / ascii / keepatt read
    a file named keepatt and stopped. A keyword there is now a keyword.
  - The outside zones need itp1: after read / avs, resetpts / itp.

